            No host networking was changed at any point. 192.168.10.2 with MAC
            00:11:22:33:44:01 is a scapy fiction, not a host address.
  tools   : tools/arpleg.py on tb277 -- one leg starts a capture on each NIC named,
            sends a known count of crafted frames, stops, decodes, and prints a grouped
            count carrying the Ethernet src/dst of every flow; it exits non-zero if its
            own send count and the sending NIC's capture disagree.
            tools/cfg.py and tools/ckcon.py drive the console (cfg.py stops its batch on
            a `% ` line); tools/rc2cfg.py saved swi_d.cfg; tools/qmark.py ran the
            read-only `?` probes; tools/ckreload.py drove the reload.

  Method: every leg sends crafted frames and counts what crosses the DUT on the far
  wire -- nothing rests on `show arp`, which on this build does not list unresolved
  entries at all (through every baseline leg below, with the DUT actively ARPing for
  both targets, the table stayed empty). Each measurement leg carries its own control
  in the SAME leg: a second address of the same shape with no entry, so a change is
  attributable to the entry and not to anything else between the legs.

